{{nihongo|'''Aoyama'''|青山都|Aoyama-to}} is the largest city and metropolis of [[Nakamizu]]. 

Located within the eastern end of [[Shichika Plains]] and Shirakawa Bay in [[Nagashima (Nakamizu)|Nagashima Island]], Aoyama has population of 11,940,022 by June 2011 with annual growth of +1.72% (2011). [[Greater Aoyama|Aoyama Metropolitan area]] has population of 33 millions people making it as the largest metropolitan of Nakamizu. Aoyama has surpassed the [[Greater Katajima-Miyagami|Katajima-Miyagami Metropolitan Area]] in 2019, earlier than the anticipated date of 2020.

With high life standard and major international economy hub. Aoyama ranks ?? in Adonia Most liveable city (2013), 10 in Global Economy Index, and considered as an [[wikipedia:Global city|alpha+ city]]. 
